  "term": "Cognitive Emotion Regulation Questionnaire",
  "definition": "The Cognitive Emotion Regulation Questionnaire is a psychological assessment tool used to measure how people think about and mentally manage negative or stressful life events. It is intended to capture a range of cognitive emotion-regulation strategies, including more adaptive and more maladaptive responses, although research has raised concerns about how clearly its proposed subscales function as separate factors.",
